COMMAND "Add a Deployable Cloud Site Template" DESCRIPTION "Birth a complete deployable cloud site template in one run: a full Astro static starter tree under templates/<slug>/ (manifest + schema + seed + app skeleton, 13 files) PLUS every catalog-family and deploy-axis wiring point — the Elixir launch allowlist, the /new display catalog, the Site closed set, the DeployRequest enum + message, the Provisioner registry row, the runtime.exs env override, the Go exact-set lock, both cloud lock-test literals, the bp CLI usage line and the MANIFEST.md entry — 13 injections across 12 files, closed by the repo's own drift gates. The historical add-a-starter path (1eec860ac, the self-described worn 9-file lockstep) left runtime.exs and the CLI usage drifted; this command carries ALL the touch points or none." LAST_UPDATED "18-07-2026-08-00-00" DOMAIN "barkpark" TAGS "templates", "cloud", "scaffold" CONCEPT "site-template" VARIANT "astro" DIRECTION "add" VARIABLES
  VARIABLE 1 "TemplateName" TITLE "Template slug" DESCRIPTION "The template's slug — lowercase kebab, conventionally ending in -starter. Drives the templates/{{.template-name}}/ tree, every allowlist entry, the Astro base path /sites/{{.template-name}}/, and the Provisioner atom + config key in its snake spelling {{.template_name}}. Pick it like an API name: it is a filesystem path on every deploy box and a closed-enum member on three surfaces." EXAMPLES "field-notes-starter", "docs-starter"
  VARIABLE 2 "TemplateTitle" OPAQUE TITLE "Human title" DESCRIPTION "The display title the /new catalog and the template manifest carry. OPAQUE: emitted verbatim (spaces + capitals preserved), spelled {{.TemplateTitle}} everywhere. No double quotes." EXAMPLES "Field Notes Starter", "Docs Starter"
  VARIABLE 3 "Description" OPAQUE TITLE "One-line description" DESCRIPTION "One sentence for the manifest, the /new display catalog, the package.json and the MANIFEST.md entry. OPAQUE verbatim prose — no double quotes, no braces, no newlines (it lands inside JSON and Elixir string literals)." EXAMPLES "A minimal static field-notes site: dated entries rendered as a list plus detail pages, pre-built by Astro at deploy time."
  VARIABLE 4 "DocType" TITLE "Content document type" DESCRIPTION "The document type this site builds from — the schema name, the seed _type, the manifest publishType and the BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE literal. Lowercase; prefer a single word (the Pascal spelling {{.DocType}} becomes the schema title). The persisted _type discriminator documents queries forever." EXAMPLES "note", "article"
  VARIABLE 5 "Theme" OPAQUE ONEOF "charple", "ember", "evergreen", "fjord" TITLE "Default palette" DESCRIPTION "The shipped palette this template defaults to — the manifest theme field and the baked data-bp-theme attribute. Must be one of the four shipped palettes (design/themes/<name>.json, mirrored by the manifest schema enum and Site.@known_site_themes); ONEOF refuses anything else at substitution time." EXAMPLES "evergreen"
  VARIABLE 6 "EnvKey" OPAQUE TITLE "Template-dir env override key" DESCRIPTION "The per-starter template-dir override env var for api/config/runtime.exs. Convention: BARKPARK_<SLUG_AS_UPPER_SNAKE>_TEMPLATE_DIR (scaffy has no upper-snake transform, so the key crosses as a declared OPAQUE literal — the add-migration timestamp precedent). Uppercase ASCII + underscores only." EXAMPLES "BARKPARK_FIELD_NOTES_STARTER_TEMPLATE_DIR", "BARKPARK_DOCS_STARTER_TEMPLATE_DIR"

# =============================================================================
# add-site-template — one command, the WHOLE worn add-a-starter path.
#
# WHAT A "SITE TEMPLATE" IS. templates/<slug>/ carrying barkpark.template.json
# is BOTH:
#   * a CATALOG template (dwb-4): the manifest + schemas/ + seed are mirrored
#     into the Go provisioner's go:embed catalog and drive the /new?template=
#     new-instance bootstrap — allowlisted in cloud Registry.@known_templates,
#     displayed by cloud Templates.@catalog, exact-set-locked by
#     TestCatalogCarriesTheShippedTemplates and BOTH directions of
#     TestEmbeddedCatalogMatchesRepoRoot;
#   * a DEPLOYABLE STARTER (search-template D7): the whole dir is the app tree
#     the box Provisioner materializes into <sites_dir>/<slug>/src — closed-enum
#     on api DeployRequest.validate_template/1, registered in the Provisioner
#     @templates map, env-overridable via runtime.exs, mirrored by cloud
#     Site.@known_site_templates and enumerated in the bp CLI usage line.
#
# ALL-OR-NOTHING, BY DESIGN. A barkpark.template.json that exists WITHOUT the
# full family reds the reverse-drift half of TestEmbeddedCatalogMatchesRepoRoot
# ("repo template not in the embedded catalog") and desyncs the three Elixir
# allowlists from the Go lock. That is exactly why this is one command: every
# touch point lands in one run, and the closing ASSERT CMD gates prove the
# family is complete before the run reports green. The engine's transactional
# refusal (any anchor miss ⇒ exit 5, nothing written) is the other half of the
# same guarantee.
#
# THE FAMILY, file by file (● create, ○ inject):
#
#   ● templates/{{.template-name}}/…                              13 files
#   ○ cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry.ex                        launch allowlist
#   ○ cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/templates.ex                       /new display catalog
#   ○ cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry/site.ex                   site-create closed set
#   ○ cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs       ×2 lock literals
#   ○ cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/sites_deploy_test.exs             message literal
#   ○ api/lib/barkpark/sites/deploy_request.ex                    ×2 enum clause + message
#   ○ api/lib/barkpark/sites/provisioner.ex                       template registry row
#   ○ api/config/runtime.exs                                      env override
#   ○ internal/provisioner/catalog/catalog_test.go                Go exact-set lock
#   ○ internal/cli/cloud_site_cmd.go                              usage enumeration
#   ○ templates/MANIFEST.md                                       manifest index entry
#
# The go:embed mirror (internal/provisioner/catalog/templates/) is NOT created
# here — `make provisioner-catalog-sync` below derives it from the repo-root
# tree (one truth; the Makefile loop is glob-driven, so it needs no edit).
#
# HONEST SCOPE — where the line falls:
#   * FRAMEWORK IS FIXED: astro, static engine. The app skeleton is a real
#     Astro tree (modeled on templates/astro-starter, the live static-engine
#     exemplar); a Next.js/node or Phoenix column of the theme×framework matrix
#     needs its own skeleton variant (site-template/nextjs) — the injection
#     block below is framework-agnostic and transplants verbatim.
#   * NO package-lock.json. The static deploy engine builds with `npm ci`,
#     which requires a lockfile scaffy cannot honestly synthesize (resolved
#     dependency hashes). MANUAL COMPLETION STEP, after the run:
#         cd templates/{{.template-name}} && npm install --package-lock-only
#     and commit the lockfile. Until then the template is catalog-complete and
#     bootstrap-complete but a box deploy fails at BUILD.
#   * SIBLING ACCRETION: the ten mark-planting inserts accrete cleanly (each
#     anchors a stable head/comment line). The three string-literal REPLACEs
#     (DeployRequest message, sites_deploy_test message, CLI usage) consume
#     their structural anchor, so a SECOND template run refuses loud (exit 5)
#     at those ops on a tree that already carries a first — re-run them by hand
#     against the grown literal, or re-anchor. Documented, not hidden.
#   * REMOVE: `bp scaffy remove` reverses the 13 creates + 13 injections
#     byte-clean, then run `make provisioner-catalog-sync` once more — the
#     sync is a true mirror (rm -rf + re-copy), so it prunes the embedded
#     copies the apply-time sync materialized.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1/13 ● Template manifest — the file whose PRESENCE binds the whole family
#     (the reverse-drift lock keys on it). Shape mirrors astro-search-starter:
#     framework astro, a shipped-palette theme, one schema, a mutations seed
#     published as {{.doc_type}}, and the starter env contract.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/barkpark.template.json"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} manifest :::
{
  "$schema": "../barkpark.template.schema.json",
  "manifestVersion": "1",
  "name": "{{.template-name}}",
  "title": "{{.TemplateTitle}}",
  "description": "{{.Description}}",
  "framework": "astro",
  "dataset": "production",
  "demoContent": true,
  "theme": "{{.Theme}}",
  "schemas": ["schemas/{{.doc_type}}.json"],
  "seed": {
    "path": "seed.json",
    "format": "mutations",
    "publish": true,
    "publishType": "{{.doc_type}}"
  },
  "env": [
    { "key": "BARKPARK_API_URL", "role": "server", "source": "api_url", "description": "Barkpark API base the BUILD reads from (the deployed site carries no token)." },
    { "key": "BARKPARK_TOKEN", "role": "server", "source": "read_token", "description": "Read-only token used at build time only." },
    { "key": "BARKPARK_DATASET", "role": "server", "source": "dataset", "description": "Dataset the build reads." },
    { "key": "BARKPARK_WORKSPACE", "role": "server", "source": "workspace", "description": "Workspace slug for scoped reads." },
    { "key": "BARKPARK_PROJECT", "role": "server", "source": "project", "description": "Project slug for scoped reads." },
    { "key": "BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE", "role": "server", "source": "literal", "value": "{{.doc_type}}", "description": "The content type the site builds from — the seeded {{.doc_type}} corpus." }
  ]
}
::: {{.template-name}} manifest :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2/13 ● Schema — the {{.doc_type}} document type (blog-starter post shape:
#     slug/excerpt/body/date), applied in order by the bootstrap.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/schemas/{{.doc_type}}.json"
WITH
::: {{.doc_type}} schema :::
{
  "name": "{{.doc_type}}",
  "title": "{{.DocType}}",
  "icon": "file-text",
  "visibility": "public",
  "fields": [
    { "name": "slug", "title": "Slug", "type": "string" },
    { "name": "excerpt", "title": "Excerpt", "type": "text" },
    { "name": "body", "title": "Body", "type": "text" },
    { "name": "published_at", "title": "Published at", "type": "string" }
  ]
}
::: {{.doc_type}} schema :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3/13 ● Seed — three published {{.doc_type}} documents (mutations format;
#     createOrReplace writes DRAFTS, so the manifest's publish+publishType do
#     the separate publish mutation — the MANIFEST.md §seed.format contract).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/seed.json"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} seed :::
{
  "mutations": [
    { "createOrReplace": { "_id": "{{.doc_type}}-welcome", "_type": "{{.doc_type}}", "title": "Welcome", "status": "published",
      "slug": "welcome",
      "excerpt": "Your new Barkpark-backed site is live.",
      "body": "This document is seeded content. Edit it in Studio, publish, and redeploy - the site rebuilds against fresh content at every deploy.",
      "published_at": "2026-01-01" } },

    { "createOrReplace": { "_id": "{{.doc_type}}-writing-in-studio", "_type": "{{.doc_type}}", "title": "Writing in Studio", "status": "published",
      "slug": "writing-in-studio",
      "excerpt": "How content flows from Studio to this site.",
      "body": "Create a {{.doc_type}}, fill in the fields the schema defines, and publish. The build reads only published documents, so drafts never leak.",
      "published_at": "2026-01-02" } },

    { "createOrReplace": { "_id": "{{.doc_type}}-how-deploys-work", "_type": "{{.doc_type}}", "title": "How deploys work", "status": "published",
      "slug": "how-deploys-work",
      "excerpt": "Static builds, health-gated, atomically switched.",
      "body": "Every deploy builds the whole site from the dataset, bakes deploy markers into the HTML, health-gates the output, and switches a symlink. Rollback is the same switch, backwards.",
      "published_at": "2026-01-03" } }
  ]
}
::: {{.template-name}} seed :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4/13 ● README — quick start + the env contract pointer.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/README.md"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} readme :::
# {{.TemplateTitle}}

{{.Description}}

A [Barkpark](https://barkpark.cloud) site template: an [Astro](https://astro.build)
site that reads its `{{.doc_type}}` documents from a Barkpark dataset **at build
time** and produces plain static HTML — built and served next to Phoenix on the
static symlink-swap deploy engine, health-gated before it goes live.

`@barkpark/core` is framework-free; the whole content link is one small module,
`src/lib/barkpark.ts`.

## Pages

- `/` — every published `{{.doc_type}}`, newest first
- `/d/<slug>/` — one document, pre-rendered at build

A broken content link (unreachable API, bad token) **fails the build** — it
never reaches visitors. A reachable-but-empty dataset renders an honest empty
state and still builds.

## Quick start

```sh
npm install
cp .env.example .env      # fill in BARKPARK_API_URL + BARKPARK_DATASET (+ token)
npm run dev
```

The env contract (`BARKPARK_API_URL` / `BARKPARK_TOKEN` / `BARKPARK_DATASET` /
`BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE`, plus the `BARKPARK_SITE_BASE` path and the deploy markers)
is the same cross-framework contract documented in `templates/DEPLOYING.md`;
see `.env.example` for every variable, including the ambient-env shadow gotcha.

## Deploying

Generate and commit the lockfile once (`npm install --package-lock-only`) — the
deploy engine builds with `npm ci`. Then:

```sh
bp cloud site create --name {{.template-name}} --dataset <ws/proj/ds> \
  --instance <id|name> --template {{.template-name}} --deploy
```

Default palette: `{{.Theme}}` (baked as `data-bp-theme`; override per site with
`--theme`).
::: {{.template-name}} readme :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5/13 ● Env contract — astro-starter's proven .env.example, retargeted.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/.env.example"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} env example :::
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# {{.TemplateTitle}} — build-time content link
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Read ONLY at build time (Astro static output)
# inside Node — the token never reaches the browser. Same cross-framework
# contract as templates/DEPLOYING.md. Keep the names identical across adapters.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED — the SCOPED API base: <origin>/w/:workspace/p/:project
#   e.g. https://guerrilla.barkpark.cloud/w/acme/p/default
BARKPARK_API_URL=

# REQUIRED — the dataset to read from.
BARKPARK_DATASET=production

# Server-only read token. A fully public dataset can read anonymously (leave
# blank). NEVER name this with a public prefix (no PUBLIC_… / NEXT_PUBLIC_…) —
# a public-prefixed var is inlined into client JS and leaks the token.
BARKPARK_TOKEN=

# Optional — only consulted when BARKPARK_API_URL is a bare (unscoped) origin.
BARKPARK_WORKSPACE=
BARKPARK_PROJECT=

# The document type this site lists + renders.
BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE={{.doc_type}}

# The path this site is served under, behind the shared Caddy front (Astro's
# `base`). The deploy engine sets this per slug.
BARKPARK_SITE_BASE=/sites/{{.template-name}}/
# Optional public origin, only used for absolute canonical/OG URLs.
BARKPARK_SITE_ORIGIN=

# Deploy markers — injected by the deploy engine, baked into the output HTML
# for its HEALTH stage. Leave blank locally (defaults to dev/unknown).
BARKPARK_BUILD_ID=
BARKPARK_CONTENT_REV=

# ⚠️  Ambient-env shadow gotcha (live-proven): Vite gives `process.env`
# PRECEDENCE over this file, so a BARKPARK_* var exported by your shell SHADOWS
# what you put here. `unset` the ambient vars or pass values inline when
# building by hand; the deploy engine scrubs its build env for you.
::: {{.template-name}} env example :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6/13 ● .gitignore — build output, deps, local env.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/.gitignore"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} gitignore :::
# build output
dist/
# astro type generation
.astro/
# deps
node_modules/
# local env — NEVER commit real tokens
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# os / editor
.DS_Store
::: {{.template-name}} gitignore :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7/13 ● package.json — published @barkpark/core (no vendor tarballs), astro 7.
#     NO lockfile here — see the HONEST SCOPE note in the header.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/package.json"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} package json :::
{
  "name": "@barkpark/{{.template-name}}",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "description": "{{.Description}}",
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "astro dev",
    "build": "astro build",
    "preview": "astro preview"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "@barkpark/core": "1.0.0-preview.3",
    "astro": "^7.0.0"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=20"
  }
}
::: {{.template-name}} package json :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8/13 ● astro.config.mjs — static output + the PATH-under-FQDN base contract
#     (BARKPARK_SITE_BASE, normalized), astro-starter's proven resolver.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/astro.config.mjs"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} astro config :::
// @ts-check
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config'

/**
 * The path this site is served under, behind the shared Caddy front. The
 * deploy engine serves every spawned site at a PATH under the content FQDN,
 * so built asset URLs must be prefixed with `/sites/<slug>/`.
 *
 * Parameterized via `BARKPARK_SITE_BASE` so the same template, unchanged,
 * ships under any slug. Astro requires a leading AND trailing slash on `base`;
 * we normalize whatever the env carries.
 */
function resolveBase() {
  const raw = (process.env.BARKPARK_SITE_BASE || '/sites/{{.template-name}}/').trim()
  const withLead = raw.startsWith('/') ? raw : `/${raw}`
  return withLead.endsWith('/') ? withLead : `${withLead}/`
}

// https://astro.build/config
export default defineConfig({
  // Static output — reproducible, isolated builds producing plain HTML the
  // deploy engine can health-gate and atomically switch.
  output: 'static',
  base: resolveBase(),
  site: process.env.BARKPARK_SITE_ORIGIN || 'http://localhost:4321',
  build: {
    assetsPrefix: undefined,
  },
})
::: {{.template-name}} astro config :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9/13 ● tsconfig — Astro strict preset.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/tsconfig.json"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} tsconfig :::
{
  "extends": "astro/tsconfigs/strict",
  "include": [".astro/types.d.ts", "**/*"],
  "exclude": ["dist"]
}
::: {{.template-name}} tsconfig :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10/13 ● The content link — build-time only, list + single fetch, honest
#     field access (top-level OR content{}-nested, both live shapes).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/lib/barkpark.ts"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} content link :::
// Build-time Barkpark content link. Runs ONLY at build (Astro static output)
// inside Node — never in the browser. Env contract: see .env.example and
// templates/DEPLOYING.md (the same names across every framework adapter).

import {
  createClient,
  type BarkparkClient,
  type BarkparkDocument,
} from '@barkpark/core'

/** Barkpark API version this template pins its reads to. */
const API_VERSION = '2026-04-01'

export interface BpEnv {
  /** Scoped API base — `<origin>/w/:ws/p/:proj`. */
  apiUrl: string
  /** Server-only read token, or undefined for anonymous public reads. */
  token: string | undefined
  dataset: string
  workspace: string | undefined
  project: string | undefined
  docType: string
  buildId: string
  contentRev: string
}

class BpConfigError extends Error {}

function required(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv, name: string): string {
  const v = env[name]
  if (typeof v !== 'string' || v.trim().length === 0) {
    throw new BpConfigError(
      `Missing required env var ${name}. See .env.example for the full contract.`,
    )
  }
  return v.trim()
}

/**
 * Resolve the build-time env contract. Throws when a required var is absent so
 * a misconfigured deploy fails LOUD at build — never silently shipping an
 * empty or anonymous site by accident.
 */
export function resolveEnv(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env): BpEnv {
  return {
    apiUrl: required(env, 'BARKPARK_API_URL'),
    dataset: required(env, 'BARKPARK_DATASET'),
    token: env.BARKPARK_TOKEN?.trim() || undefined,
    workspace: env.BARKPARK_WORKSPACE?.trim() || undefined,
    project: env.BARKPARK_PROJECT?.trim() || undefined,
    docType: env.BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE?.trim() || '{{.doc_type}}',
    buildId: env.BARKPARK_BUILD_ID?.trim() || 'dev',
    contentRev: env.BARKPARK_CONTENT_REV?.trim() || 'unknown',
  }
}

/** True when `url`'s path already carries a `/w/:ws/p/:proj` scope. */
function isScopedUrl(url: string): boolean {
  try {
    return /\/w\/[^/]+\/p\/[^/]+\/?$/.test(new URL(url).pathname)
  } catch {
    return false
  }
}

/**
 * A FRESH `@barkpark/core` client for this build. Deliberately NOT memoized
 * and NOT `createPreloader` (Next.js-specific; bleeds request state across
 * module scope).
 */
export function createBarkparkClient(env: BpEnv): BarkparkClient {
  const scoped = isScopedUrl(env.apiUrl)
  return createClient({
    projectUrl: env.apiUrl,
    dataset: env.dataset,
    apiVersion: API_VERSION,
    perspective: 'published',
    ...(env.token ? { token: env.token } : {}),
    ...(!scoped && env.workspace ? { workspace: env.workspace } : {}),
    ...(!scoped && env.project ? { project: env.project } : {}),
  })
}

export interface SiteDoc {
  id: string
  slug: string
  title: string
  excerpt: string
  body: string
  publishedAt: string
}

/** Read a field from either live document shape: top-level or content{}. */
function field(doc: BarkparkDocument, name: string): string {
  const flat = (doc as Record<string, unknown>)[name]
  if (typeof flat === 'string' && flat.length > 0) return flat
  const content = (doc as Record<string, unknown>).content
  if (content && typeof content === 'object') {
    const nested = (content as Record<string, unknown>)[name]
    if (typeof nested === 'string' && nested.length > 0) return nested
  }
  return ''
}

function toSiteDoc(doc: BarkparkDocument): SiteDoc | null {
  if (typeof doc._id !== 'string' || doc._id.length === 0) return null
  const title = field(doc, 'title') || doc._id
  return {
    id: doc._id,
    slug: field(doc, 'slug') || doc._id,
    title,
    excerpt: field(doc, 'excerpt'),
    body: field(doc, 'body'),
    publishedAt: field(doc, 'published_at'),
  }
}

/**
 * Every published document of the site's type, newest first. A network / auth
 * failure THROWS (the build fails — a broken content link must never reach
 * visitors; that is the health-gate premise). An empty dataset returns [] so
 * the site still builds an honest empty state.
 */
export async function fetchSiteDocs(
  bp: BarkparkClient,
  env: BpEnv,
): Promise<SiteDoc[]> {
  const rows = await bp
    .docs(env.docType)
    .order('_updatedAt:desc')
    .limit(200)
    .find()
  return rows
    .map(toSiteDoc)
    .filter((d): d is SiteDoc => d !== null)
}
::: {{.template-name}} content link :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11/13 ● Base layout — bakes the deploy markers the engine's HEALTH stage
#     greps for, plus the {{.Theme}} palette hook (data-bp-theme).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/layouts/Base.astro"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} base layout :::
---
/**
 * Base HTML shell. Bakes the deploy markers the deploy engine greps for in its
 * HEALTH stage (bp-build-id / bp-content-rev / bp-doc-id / bp-doc-title), so a
 * build that lost its content link never passes health and never goes live.
 */
export interface Props {
  title: string
  buildId: string
  contentRev: string
  docId: string
  docTitle: string
}

const { title, buildId, contentRev, docId, docTitle } = Astro.props
const siteBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-bp-theme="{{.Theme}}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta name="bp-build-id" content={buildId} />
    <meta name="bp-content-rev" content={contentRev} />
    <meta name="bp-doc-id" content={docId} />
    <meta name="bp-doc-title" content={docTitle} />
    <meta name="bp-site-base" content={siteBase} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <style is:global>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
        --bg: #ffffff;
        --fg: #16181d;
        --muted: #5b6472;
        --card: #f6f7f9;
        --border: #e4e7ec;
        --accent: #3b5bdb;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --bg: #0e1117;
          --fg: #e6e9ef;
          --muted: #99a2b2;
          --card: #171b23;
          --border: #262c37;
          --accent: #7c93f5;
        }
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--fg);
        font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
      }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <slot />
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
::: {{.template-name}} base layout :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12/13 ● Index page — every published {{.doc_type}}, newest first, linking
#     into the pre-rendered detail pages under the site base.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/pages/index.astro"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} index page :::
---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { resolveEnv, createBarkparkClient, fetchSiteDocs } from '../lib/barkpark'

// Build time only. A missing required env var or a broken content link throws
// here and fails the build loudly — it never reaches visitors.
const env = resolveEnv()
const bp = createBarkparkClient(env)
const docs = await fetchSiteDocs(bp, env)
const newest = docs[0]

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<Base
  title="{{.TemplateTitle}}"
  buildId={env.buildId}
  contentRev={env.contentRev}
  docId={newest?.id ?? ''}
  docTitle={newest?.title ?? ''}
>
  <header>
    <p style="margin:0 0 .25rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">
      Barkpark Cloud · Astro
    </p>
    <h1 style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;font-size:2rem;line-height:1.2;">{{.TemplateTitle}}</h1>
  </header>

  {
    docs.length > 0 ? (
      <ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:1rem;">
        {docs.map((doc) => (
          <li style="border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--card);border-radius:12px;padding:1.25rem;">
            <h2 style="margin:0 0 .35rem;font-size:1.2rem;">
              <a href={`${base}d/${doc.slug}/`} style="text-decoration:none;color:inherit;">
                {doc.title}
              </a>
            </h2>
            {doc.excerpt && (
              <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem;color:var(--muted);">{doc.excerpt}</p>
            )}
            <p style="margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;">
              {doc.publishedAt && <span>{doc.publishedAt} · </span>}
              <code>{doc.id}</code>
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <article style="border:1px dashed var(--border);border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;color:var(--muted);">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--fg);">
          No <code>{env.docType}</code> documents yet
        </h2>
        <p style="margin:0;">
          The content link is live, but this dataset has no published
          <code>{env.docType}</code> documents. Publish one in Barkpark and
          redeploy — the site rebuilds against fresh content.
        </p>
      </article>
    )
  }

  <footer style="margin-top:2.5rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;">
    <p style="margin:0;">
      build <code>{env.buildId}</code> · content rev <code>{env.contentRev}</code>
    </p>
  </footer>
</Base>
::: {{.template-name}} index page :::

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 13/13 ● Detail page — one static route per published {{.doc_type}}
#     (getStaticPaths params must be plain strings).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/pages/d/[slug].astro"
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} detail page :::
---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import {
  resolveEnv,
  createBarkparkClient,
  fetchSiteDocs,
  type SiteDoc,
} from '../../lib/barkpark'

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const env = resolveEnv()
  const bp = createBarkparkClient(env)
  const docs = await fetchSiteDocs(bp, env)
  // Slug values must be plain strings; each doc becomes one pre-rendered page.
  return docs.map((doc) => ({ params: { slug: doc.slug }, props: { doc } }))
}

interface Props {
  doc: SiteDoc
}

const { doc } = Astro.props
const env = resolveEnv()
const paragraphs = doc.body
  .split(/\n\s*\n/)
  .map((p) => p.trim())
  .filter((p) => p.length > 0)

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<Base
  title={doc.title}
  buildId={env.buildId}
  contentRev={env.contentRev}
  docId={doc.id}
  docTitle={doc.title}
>
  <nav style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;">
    <a href={base} style="font-size:.9rem;">← All entries</a>
  </nav>

  <article>
    <h1 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:2rem;line-height:1.2;">{doc.title}</h1>
    <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;">
      {doc.publishedAt && <span>{doc.publishedAt} · </span>}
      <code>{doc.id}</code>
    </p>
    {paragraphs.map((p) => (
      <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">{p}</p>
    ))}
  </article>
</Base>
::: {{.template-name}} detail page :::

# =============================================================================
# INJECTIONS — the catalog family + the deploy axis, one guarded mark each.
# Mark shape: st--<slug>--<site> (variable part FIRST, static tail LAST — the
# tier-<name>--<tier> prefix-safety pattern: st--docs--known is never a
# substring of st--docs-starter--known, so the engine's substring re-run guard
# cannot false-skip a sibling).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud launch allowlist — Registry.@known_templates (head of list; the Go
#   exact-set lock compares as a set, cloud lock literals ride below).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry.ex"
### Allowlist the slug for /v1/launch template validation
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: known-templates head :::
    # new content-template slugs land here (head of list)
::: known-templates head :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} known entry :::
    # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--known
    "{{.template-name}}",
::: {{.template-name}} known entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--known"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud /new display catalog — Templates.@catalog (head of list; slugs/0
#   must stay list-equal to Registry.known_templates/0, and both ops insert at
#   the head, so the lock holds by construction). The description is emitted in
#   mix format's canonical broken form — canonical for descriptions ≥ ~77
#   chars; a very short one joins under the advisory Format gate (cosmetic).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/templates.ex"
### Display card for the /new?template= launch flow
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: catalog opener :::
  @catalog [
::: catalog opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} catalog card :::
    # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--catalog
    %{
      slug: "{{.template-name}}",
      title: "{{.TemplateTitle}}",
      description:
        "{{.Description}}",
      framework: "astro",
      demo_content: true,
      what_you_get: [
        "An `{{.doc_type}}` content type — slug, excerpt, body, date",
        "A static Astro site: index list + per-document detail pages, pre-rendered at build",
        "Demo {{.doc_type}} documents seeded so it renders on first deploy",
        "Symlink-swap deploys: immutable releases, health-gated, instant rollback"
      ],
      env_keys: @env_common ++ ~w(BARKPARK_DOC_TYPE),
      repo: @repo,
      docs: @docs
    },
::: {{.template-name}} catalog card :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--catalog"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud site-create closed set — Site.@known_site_templates (head of list;
#   the validation message enumerates in declaration order, so the test
#   literal REPLACE below matches head-first).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry/site.ex"
### Allow the slug on POST /v1/sites (bp cloud site create --template)
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: site-templates head :::
    # new deployable site-template slugs land here (head of list)
::: site-templates head :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} site entry :::
    # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--site
    "{{.template-name}}",
::: {{.template-name}} site entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--site"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud lock literal #1 — the 422 unknown-template body (order = the
#   registry's declaration order, so the new slug lands at the head).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs"
### Extend the unknown-template 422 body literal
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: unknown-template body opener :::
      assert body["known_templates"] == [
::: unknown-template body opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} bootstrap body entry :::
               # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-known
               "{{.template-name}}",
::: {{.template-name}} bootstrap body entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-known"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud lock literal #2 — the known_templates/0 mirror test ("change BOTH
#   together" — this IS the both).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs"
### Extend the catalog-mirror lock literal
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: mirror lock opener :::
    assert Registry.known_templates() == [
::: mirror lock opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} mirror entry :::
             # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-mirror
             "{{.template-name}}",
::: {{.template-name}} mirror entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-mirror"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ cloud site-create message literal — sites_deploy_test pins the exact
#   validation message; the new slug enumerates first (declaration order).
#   MARK VIRTUAL: a string literal admits no comment. Sibling accretion: a
#   second template consumes this anchor — see HONEST SCOPE.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/sites_deploy_test.exs"
### Extend the pinned site-template validation message
REPLACE
::: site message anchor :::
      assert {"must be one of: astro-search-starter, astro-starter, next-starter, search-starter",
::: site message anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} site message :::
      assert {"must be one of: {{.template-name}}, astro-search-starter, astro-starter, next-starter, search-starter",
::: {{.template-name}} site message :::
MARK VIRTUAL "st--{{.template-name}}--deploy-test-msg"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "must be one of: {{.template-name}},"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ api deploy enum — DeployRequest.validate_template/1: one clause before the
#   catch-all (closed set: the value indexes a filesystem path, never
#   String.to_atom on request data).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "api/lib/barkpark/sites/deploy_request.ex"
### Accept the slug on POST /v1/admin/site-deploy
INSERT BEFORE FIRST
::: validate-template catch-all :::
  defp validate_template(_template),
::: validate-template catch-all :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} deploy clause :::
  # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--deploy-request
  defp validate_template("{{.template-name}}"), do: {:ok, :{{.template_name}}}

::: {{.template-name}} deploy clause :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--deploy-request"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ api deploy enum message — the invalid_template hint enumerates every legal
#   slug. MARK VIRTUAL (string literal); sibling accretion consumes the anchor.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "api/lib/barkpark/sites/deploy_request.ex"
### Extend the invalid_template message enumeration
REPLACE
::: deploy message anchor :::
       ~s(template must be one of "astro-starter", "next-starter", "search-starter", "astro-search-starter")}
::: deploy message anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} deploy message :::
       ~s(template must be one of "astro-starter", "next-starter", "search-starter", "astro-search-starter", "{{.template-name}}")}
::: {{.template-name}} deploy message :::
MARK VIRTUAL "st--{{.template-name}}--deploy-request-msg"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN ", \"{{.template-name}}\")"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ api provisioner registry — @templates row: the atom the enum clause mints
#   maps to its config-override key + repo-relative source dir.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "api/lib/barkpark/sites/provisioner.ex"
### Register the template dir in the Provisioner registry
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: templates map opener :::
  @templates %{
::: templates map opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} provisioner row :::
    # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--provisioner
    {{.template_name}}: {:{{.template_name}}_template_dir, "templates/{{.template-name}}"},
::: {{.template-name}} provisioner row :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--provisioner"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ api runtime config — the per-starter template-dir env override (the touch
#   point the historical astro-search-starter addition MISSED — live drift,
#   benign only via the module default fallback). Emitted single-line, the
#   house shape; a slug ≥ ~18 chars pushes the line past mix format's 98-col
#   wrap and advisory-reds the Format job — cosmetic, `mix format
#   config/runtime.exs` re-wraps it (deploy_request.ex:62 carries the same
#   pre-existing debt on main).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "api/config/runtime.exs"
### Wire the env override into the Provisioner runtime config
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: provisioner env opener :::
      sites_dir: System.get_env("BARKPARK_SITES_DIR"),
::: provisioner env opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} runtime override :::
      # scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--runtime
      {{.template_name}}_template_dir: System.get_env("{{.EnvKey}}"),
::: {{.template-name}} runtime override :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--runtime"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ Go exact-set lock — catalog_test.go `want` (append-friendly: sorted before
#   compare, so head insertion is order-safe).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "internal/provisioner/catalog/catalog_test.go"
### Extend the Go embedded-catalog exact-set lock
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: want opener :::
	want := []string{
::: want opener :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} want entry :::
		// scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--catalog-test
		"{{.template-name}}",
::: {{.template-name}} want entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--catalog-test"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ bp CLI usage — the --template enumeration in `bp cloud site create`.
#   MARK VIRTUAL (string literal); sibling accretion consumes the anchor.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "internal/cli/cloud_site_cmd.go"
### Enumerate the slug in the CLI usage line
REPLACE
::: cli usage anchor :::
	const usage = "bp cloud site create --name <n> --dataset <ws/proj/ds> --instance <id|name> [--framework astro] [--kind static|node] [--doc-type <type>] [--template astro-starter|next-starter|search-starter|astro-search-starter] [--deploy]"
::: cli usage anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} cli usage :::
	const usage = "bp cloud site create --name <n> --dataset <ws/proj/ds> --instance <id|name> [--framework astro] [--kind static|node] [--doc-type <type>] [--template astro-starter|next-starter|search-starter|astro-search-starter|{{.template-name}}] [--deploy]"
::: {{.template-name}} cli usage :::
MARK VIRTUAL "st--{{.template-name}}--cli-usage"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "|{{.template-name}}]"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ○ MANIFEST.md — the human index of retrofitted manifests.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IN "templates/MANIFEST.md"
### Index the template in MANIFEST.md
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: manifest index anchor :::
  the static symlink-swap engine.
::: manifest index anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.template-name}} manifest entry :::
- `templates/{{.template-name}}/` — {{.Description}} (scaffy
  `add-site-template` instance: Astro static, `{{.doc_type}}` type,
  `{{.Theme}}` default palette.)
  <!-- scaffy:add-site-template {{.TemplateName}} MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--manifest-md -->
::: {{.template-name}} manifest entry :::
MARK "st--{{.template-name}}--manifest-md"

# =============================================================================
# Post-conditions — every family member present, then the repo's OWN drift
# gates as the close: the completeness of the family IS the correctness.
# =============================================================================
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/barkpark.template.json" CONTAINS "\"name\": \"{{.template-name}}\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/barkpark.template.json" CONTAINS "\"publishType\": \"{{.doc_type}}\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/schemas/{{.doc_type}}.json" CONTAINS "\"name\": \"{{.doc_type}}\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/seed.json" CONTAINS "\"_id\": \"{{.doc_type}}-welcome\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/README.md" CONTAINS "# {{.TemplateTitle}}"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/.env.example" CONTAINS "BARKPARK_SITE_BASE=/sites/{{.template-name}}/"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/.gitignore" EXISTS
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/package.json" CONTAINS "\"name\": \"@barkpark/{{.template-name}}\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/astro.config.mjs" CONTAINS "/sites/{{.template-name}}/"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/tsconfig.json" CONTAINS "astro/tsconfigs/strict"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/lib/barkpark.ts" CONTAINS "fetchSiteDocs"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/layouts/Base.astro" CONTAINS "data-bp-theme=\"{{.Theme}}\""
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/pages/index.astro" CONTAINS "fetchSiteDocs"
ASSERT FILE "templates/{{.template-name}}/src/pages/d/[slug].astro" CONTAINS "getStaticPaths"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--known"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/templates.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--catalog"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/lib/barkpark_cloud/registry/site.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--site"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-known"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--bootstrap-mirror"
ASSERT FILE "cloud/test/barkpark_cloud/sites_deploy_test.exs" CONTAINS "must be one of: {{.template-name}},"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/sites/deploy_request.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--deploy-request"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/sites/deploy_request.ex" CONTAINS ", \"{{.template-name}}\")"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/sites/provisioner.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--provisioner"
ASSERT FILE "api/config/runtime.exs" CONTAINS "System.get_env(\"{{.EnvKey}}\")"
ASSERT FILE "internal/provisioner/catalog/catalog_test.go" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--catalog-test"
ASSERT FILE "internal/cli/cloud_site_cmd.go" CONTAINS "|{{.template-name}}]"
ASSERT FILE "templates/MANIFEST.md" CONTAINS "MARK:st--{{.template-name}}--manifest-md"

# The repo's own gates close the run. LOCAL: the go:embed mirror sync (a fast
# rm-and-copy; glob-driven, so it needs no Makefile edit) + the Go catalog
# lock (BOTH drift directions + manifest Load/Validate of the new template) +
# a vet over the CLI edit. TIER ci: the Elixir gates — the api suite compiles
# the world (A2), and the cloud lock tests need a local Postgres; both run on
# every PR. (Proven warm-locally 2026-07-18: cloud scoped mix test, 52 tests
# in ~6s with CC=/usr/bin/clang — run it yourself when you carry a warm
# cloud/_build and a test DB.)
ASSERT CMD "make provisioner-catalog-sync"
ASSERT CMD "CC=/usr/bin/clang go test ./internal/provisioner/catalog/ -count=1"
ASSERT CMD "CC=/usr/bin/clang go vet ./internal/cli/"
ASSERT CMD "cd cloud && CC=/usr/bin/clang mix test test/barkpark_cloud/bootstrap_template_test.exs test/barkpark_cloud/web/router_templates_test.exs test/barkpark_cloud/sites_deploy_test.exs" TIER ci
ASSERT CMD "cd api && CC=/usr/bin/clang mix test test/barkpark/sites/deploy_runner_test.exs" TIER ci
